---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL, PORTFOLIO_URL, REPO_URL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About · Tony Duong"
			description="Tony Duong, fullstack and AI engineer in Bordeaux: who I am, what I work on, and how these field notes are made."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="wrap">
			<h1>About</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				Fullstack and AI engineer with seven years of experience, based in Bordeaux. Comfortable from
				architecture scoping to production, and most interested in the part where a system meets
				real money, real servers and real users.
			</p>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>What I work on</h2>
				<p>
					Since January 2024 I am partner and tech lead at Econumerica. The core of my work there is
					a non-custodial DeFi platform spread across several repositories: a NestJS backend, MiniDapps
					running on Minima nodes, and positions on EVM chains through Uniswap, THORChain and Maya.
					That is where most of the on-chain and Minima notes come from: multisig custody signed node by
					node, LP accounting, fund valuation that must never turn a failed read into a zero.
				</p>
				<p>
					I also run the servers these systems live on. Docker, Traefik and Dokploy on a handful of
					hosts, backups that prove their restore, migrations rehearsed on a copy of production. And I
					write most of my code with Claude Code, in production conditions, with the cost and the
					leaks measured rather than guessed.
				</p>
				<p>
					Before that: JavaScript developer at Amiltone (Vue 3, TypeScript, Node, ElasticSearch) and
					junior web developer at TEHTRIS, a cybersecurity company, on Vue 2 and 3. I hold an MSc in
					AI and Big Data project management (IA School), and a DUT in computer science plus the DAWIN
					diploma from IUT Bordeaux. The AI governance side, EU AI Act included, is part of how I scope
					anything that ships a model to users.
				</p>

				<h2>In the open</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<a href="https://rag-quest.vercel.app">RAG Quest</a> and
						<a href="https://angular-quest-game.vercel.app">Angular Quest</a>, two open-source learning
						games (data, NLP and retrieval; modern Angular), with the code on GitHub.
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://github.com/tonystechofficial/claude-code-guide-de-terrain">A field guide to
						Claude Code</a>, in French, under CC BY 4.0.
					</li>
					<li>
						Two products under the devanchor brand: Régie, a social scheduling tool forked from Postiz,
						and Skilance, a freelance marketplace. Both are paused while I decide what deserves the
						next push.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 id="how">How these notes are made</h2>
				<p>
					Every post starts from the working notes I keep while doing the job. The notes hold the
					measurement: the command that was run, the number that came back, the error message as it
					was printed. A post is dated by the day that work happened, not by the day it was published,
					and it says so at the bottom.
				</p>
				<p>
					I draft the English text with Claude Code from those notes and edit it myself. Nothing here
					reproduces a client's code or data. Hosts, identifiers and client names are removed, and a
					fact that the notes do not support is left out rather than filled in.
				</p>

				<h2>Elsewhere</h2>
				<p>
					<a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a> · <a href={PORTFOLIO_URL}>Portfolio</a> ·
					<a href="mailto:astowny@gmail.com">astowny@gmail.com</a> ·
					<a href={REPO_URL}>source of this site</a>
				</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
